---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility — Jordan Krueger"
  description="How I approach accessibility on jordankrueger.com and how to report a barrier."
>
  <section class="section bg-white">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 720px;">
      <h1>Accessibility</h1>
      <p style="opacity: 0.7;">Last updated: June 8, 2026</p>

      <p>I want jordankrueger.com to work for everyone, including people who use screen readers, keyboard navigation, or other assistive technology.</p>

      <h2>What I aim for</h2>
      <p>I build toward the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at the AA level: readable color contrast, pages you can navigate by keyboard, real text alternatives for images, a logical heading order, and a visible skip-to-content link.</p>

      <h2>Where it stands</h2>
      <p>I maintain this site myself, so treat it as a work in progress rather than a certified result. Some embedded third-party content, like SoundCloud players, brings its own controls that I don't fully govern.</p>

      <h2>Found a barrier?</h2>
      <p>If something here is hard to use with assistive technology, I'd genuinely like to hear about it. Tell me which page and what got in your way through the <a href="/#contact">contact form</a>, and I'll fix what I can.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
